# Fivvle.io — Cursor Project Rules

## Project Overview

Fivvle.io is an AI-powered startup idea validation platform. Founders submit ideas; the system runs cognitive validation (AI refinement + multi-step agentic market research) and lightweight behavioral validation (auto-generated tracked landing pages with waitlist conversion + source-tag analytics).

The project has three authoritative reference documents at the project root:
- `ARCHITECTURE.md` — technical contract: data model, state machine, component architecture, sequence diagrams, trust boundaries, ADRs.
- `USER_FLOW.md` — product contract: complete founder journey across 8 stages.
- `AGENTS.md` — security rules. Non-negotiable. If guidance there conflicts with this file, AGENTS.md wins.

Architectural decision history lives in `docs/adr/`. Read these when reasoning about why something is the way it is.

Always reference the relevant document when generating code. Match class names, state names, sequence steps, and stage numbers exactly.

## Architectural Choice: Modular Monolith

Fivvle uses a **modular monolith**, NOT microservices. Documented in ARCHITECTURE.md ADR and `docs/adr/0001-modular-monolith.md`.

- One FastAPI codebase for user-facing API
- Cloud Functions for long-running background work (research engine, insight generator, auto-archive) — targeted process isolation, NOT a path toward microservices
- Service-to-service calls within backend are Python function calls, not HTTP
- Do NOT propose Kafka, RabbitMQ, gRPC, service mesh, or splitting FastAPI into multiple services

## MVP Scope (binding)

**In scope:**
- AI idea refinement
- Multi-step agentic AI research engine (5 phases) over Tavily + Reddit free tier + Google Trends + news
- Validation report with structured findings and citations
- Auto-generated landing pages: 5 designer-built templates with bounded customization, ISR-cached
- Page view + source tag + waitlist signup tracking
- Insight report combining research + behavior
- Cost tracking infrastructure

**Out of scope for MVP:**
- Multi-platform video posting, comment harvesting, video upload
- Social account OAuth
- Phone verification
- Payments
- Reddit posting (read-only research only)
- TikTok integration
- Custom domains per landing page
- Free-form HTML/CSS template editing
- AI-generated landing page layouts (templates with bounded customization only)
- Phase 2 research enhancements (Exa, Firecrawl, deep multi-loop reflection)
- Truly multi-agent architecture
- Microservices, service mesh, message queues

If asked to build any out-of-scope feature, push back and ask whether the architecture documents should be updated first.

## Tech Stack

### Frontend
- Next.js 14+ App Router with TypeScript strict mode
- Tailwind CSS only (no shadcn/ui, Radix, Headless UI, MUI, etc.)
- Firebase Auth Web SDK
- Native `fetch` with typed wrapper in `lib/api.ts`
- Hosted on Vercel or Firebase App Hosting
- Public landing pages use Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR)
- No Server Actions for backend logic
- Icons: `lucide-react` (only UI library exception)
- Fonts: `next/font/google`
- Images: `next/image`

### Backend
- FastAPI on Python 3.11+
- `uv` for package management (not pip, not poetry)
- uvicorn (dev), gunicorn + uvicorn workers (prod)
- SQLAlchemy 2.0 async + asyncpg for Cloud SQL Postgres
- Alembic for migrations
- Pydantic v2 for validation, Instructor for structured LLM outputs
- Firebase Admin SDK (Python) for token verification
- Hosted on Google Cloud Run

### Background Jobs
- Python Cloud Functions (2nd gen)
- Cloud Scheduler (cron) + HTTP triggers from FastAPI
- No Celery, no Redis

### Research Engine
- Multi-step single-agent workflow with 5 phases — NOT truly multi-agent
- Plain `asyncio` + Pydantic, NOT LangGraph/AutoGen/CrewAI
- Phases: Planner → Searcher → Reader → Reflector → Synthesizer
- Total time 2-4 minutes; cost target $0.25-$0.70 per run

### LLM Layer
- Anthropic Claude for reasoning-heavy calls (refinement, all research phases, insight, landing page generation)
- Groq for high-volume low-stakes only
- All calls through `/backend/app/llm/client.py` — never import provider SDKs elsewhere
- Every call writes to `LLMCall` table

### External APIs
- Tavily — primary search/extraction
- Reddit (PRAW free tier) — read-only research only, under 60 req/min
- pytrends — Google Trends with fallback
- NOT in MVP: Exa, Firecrawl, Anthropic web search tool

### Data
- Cloud SQL Postgres (direct, NOT Firebase Data Connect)
- Firebase Auth (identity only)
- No Firestore

### Secrets
- Google Cloud Secret Manager in production
- `.env` for local dev only, never committed

