## Conventions

### Python (Backend)
- Type hints everywhere, no untyped code
- `async def` for all I/O-bound code
- Pydantic v2 for request/response, separate from SQLAlchemy `models.py`
- SQLAlchemy 2.0 syntax only (`select()`, `Mapped`, `mapped_column`)
- Ruff for lint and format
- Pydantic Settings for config

### TypeScript (Frontend)
- Strict mode always
- Default to React Server Components, Client Components only when needed
- No Server Actions for backend logic
- No client-side data fetching libraries for MVP

### API Design
- Routers thin (5-15 lines)
- Services own business logic
- Database access never leaks out of services
- Every authenticated endpoint verifies Firebase token via `Depends()`
- Every endpoint with a resource ID verifies ownership (see AGENTS.md)

### State Machine
- `Experiment.status` enum matches ARCHITECTURE.md State Machine exactly
- State transitions are explicit functions on experiment service
- Research phases are sub-states — Cloud Function updates as it transitions

### Research Engine
- `asyncio` + Pydantic, NOT a framework
- Each phase is a separate function with typed input/output
- Reflection loops cap at 1-2
- Prompts in `functions/research_engine/prompts/` as named module constants
- Each phase logs LLM call(s) to `LLMCall` with phase name
- Searches parallel within phase via `asyncio.gather()`
- Citations are first-class data
- Quality > token efficiency — use Claude for all phases

### LLM Calls
- All through `/backend/app/llm/client.py`
- Prompts in `/backend/app/llm/prompts/` or `/backend/functions/research_engine/prompts/`
- Every call MUST log to `LLMCall` table — enforced in client wrapper
- Use Instructor for structured outputs

### Cost Tracking & Limits
- `LLMCall` and `ExternalAPICall` tables capture every paid operation
- LLM client wrapper computes cost from price table in `/backend/app/llm/cost.py`
- Soft limits enforced in code:
  - 5 refinement regenerations per experiment
  - 5 landing page field regenerations per page
  - 1-2 reflection loops in research engine
  - 6-minute hard timeout on research engine
- Per-experiment cost target: under $1.50
- Admin endpoints (NOT exposed to founders): `/admin/cost/experiment/{id}`, `/admin/cost/user/{id}`, `/admin/cost/daily`, `/admin/cost/per-phase`

---

## Frontend/Backend Boundary

For the canonical frontend/backend security boundary, see **AGENTS.md "Secrets management"** and **AGENTS.md "Frontend-specific security"** sections. Summary:

- All API keys, business logic, external API calls, LLM calls, database access live in the backend
- Frontend handles UI, Firebase Auth client, page view beacons, display of backend data only
- Streaming responses pass through backend, never direct frontend → LLM provider

## Reliability & Fault Tolerance

Fault isolation through code and process design, not service splits.

### Circuit breakers around external APIs
- Every external API call wrapped in circuit breaker
- After 5 consecutive failures, breaker opens for 60s cooldown
- Live in `/backend/app/reliability/circuit_breakers.py`

### Required timeouts
- LLM calls: 60s for refinement, 120s per research phase
- Tavily: 30s
- Reddit: 15s
- Google Trends: 15s
- DB queries: 10s default, 30s for analytics rollups
- HTTP fetches: 30s
- No call ever runs without a timeout

### Retry policy
- Exponential backoff with jitter
- Max 3 retries on transient failures
- No retries on 4xx (except 408, 429)
- Idempotency keys for any external mutation

### Graceful degradation
- Anthropic unavailable: fall back to Groq for non-critical phases (reflector); for critical phases, surface error and retry
- Tavily down: return partial results from sources that succeeded; mark report partial
- Reddit rate-limited: skip Reddit signals; note in report
- Trends flaky: retry 3x then continue without; note in report
- DB briefly unavailable: retry with backoff, fail cleanly if persistent

### Health checks
- `GET /health` — liveness
- `GET /health/ready` — readiness (DB connection, secrets loaded)

### Error tracking
- Sentry from day one (see AGENTS.md for redaction rules)
- All unhandled exceptions captured with context (user_id, experiment_id, request_id)

### Structured logging
- `structlog` for Python, structured logger for Next.js
- See AGENTS.md "Logging hygiene" for what NEVER to log

### Per-endpoint rate limits
- Authenticated: 60 req/min/user
- Public (analytics, waitlist): 30 req/min/IP
- 429 with retry-after header

## Quality Discipline

### Research Engine Quality

- **Prompt engineering is the differentiator, not architecture.** Plan 1+ week each on the planner, reader, and synthesizer prompts. Iterate against real founder ideas.
- **Eval methodology required from day one.** Maintain an eval set in `/backend/tests/eval/` of 10-20 founder ideas with "gold standard" expected reports. Run eval before shipping any prompt change.
- **Specificity over summary in synthesis.** The synthesizer prompt must produce specific quotes, specific competitor names, specific numbers, specific user complaints — not generic summaries.
- **Citations are non-negotiable.** Every claim has a source URL.
- **Source selection > source quantity.** Tavily is sufficient for MVP. Don't add more sources until usage data shows they're needed.
- **Don't downgrade models to save pennies.** Use Claude for all research phases.
- **Build a 3-phase POC first.** Before building the full 5-phase pipeline (step 8 in build order), build a minimal Tavily + planner + synthesizer version (step 7) to validate prompt quality and cost. Adding reader and reflector phases happens only after the simpler version produces reports you'd be willing to ship.

### Landing Page Quality

- Templates are designer-built, not LLM-generated.
- AI's role is bounded selection within templates, not generation.
- The default draft must look great out of the box.
- Bounded customization only. Founders pick from dropdowns and edit text inline. No HTML/CSS/component injection.
- Mobile-first. Every template tested on mobile before merge.
- Accessibility AA minimum. Color contrast, keyboard navigation, alt text, semantic HTML, visible focus states.

## Landing Page Template Implementation

### The 5 templates for MVP

| ID | Name | Best for | Mood |
|---|---|---|---|
| `minimal` | Minimal | B2B SaaS, productivity, dev tools | Confident, premium, understated |
| `vibrant` | Bold/Vibrant | Consumer, design-forward | Energetic, modern |
| `indie` | Indie | Solo founder projects, side projects | Authentic, approachable |
| `premium-dark` | Dark/Premium | Dev tools, AI products | Sleek, technical |
| `editorial` | Editorial | Content-first, social impact | Thoughtful, narrative |

### Template Stack
- React Server Components (default), Client Components only for interactive bits
- TypeScript strict mode
- Tailwind CSS only — no styled-components, no CSS modules, no plain CSS files
- No UI libraries (no shadcn/ui, Radix, Headless UI, MUI, etc.)
- `lucide-react` for icons (only allowed UI library)
- `next/font/google` for fonts
- `next/image` for images
- Plain HTML form elements styled with Tailwind
- Animations: Tailwind utilities first; Framer Motion only if necessary

### Mandatory props interface

Every template implements `LandingPageProps` and exports `metadata: TemplateMetadata` (defined in `frontend/components/landing-templates/types.ts`). See ARCHITECTURE.md for full type definitions.

